From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reindert Pelsma <reindert.pelsma@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 02:31:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: register the virtio-nvgpu sources with meson

nvkvm's device lives in hw/misc/ as eleven .c files copied in from this
repo's src/qemu/ (see docs/howto/build.md).  Meson has no globbing, so
the file list has to be written out; this adds it, plus the
include_directories() entry for hw/misc/nvkvm_inc/, which is where the
build copies src/abi/*.h and src/common/*.h so the device sources can
reach the shared ABI headers without reaching outside the QEMU tree.

CONFIG_VIRTIO gates the block because the device is a virtio device: on
a target built without virtio there is nothing for it to attach to, and
the sources would not link.

Two things a reader will notice and should not "fix" without thinking:

  * The block lands between the "# HPPA devices" comment and the
    CONFIG_LASI line it belongs to.  That is an artefact of how the
    pre-patch-series build script inserted it (before the last non-empty
    line of the file), preserved here so the patched tree is
    byte-identical to what that script produced and the migration to a
    patch series is provably a no-op.  Moving it to the end of the file
    is a safe follow-up -- do it as its own commit so the diff says so.

  * nvkvm_dispatch.c is in the list but is dead code at runtime (see
    docs/internal/audit-guest-pointers.md).  It still has to compile and
    link; dropping it from the build is a separate decision from
    dropping it from the tree.
---
 hw/misc/meson.build | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/misc/meson.build b/hw/misc/meson.build
index d02d96e..ef97efc 100644
--- a/hw/misc/meson.build
+++ b/hw/misc/meson.build
@@ -151,4 +151,20 @@ specific_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_MIPS_ITU', if_true: files('mips_itu.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_SBSA_REF', if_true: files('sbsa_ec.c'))
 
 # HPPA devices
+
+nvkvm_inc = include_directories('nvkvm_inc')
+
+system_ss.add(when: ['CONFIG_VIRTIO'], if_true: files(
+  'virtio_nvgpu.c',
+  'virtio_nvgpu_pci.c',
+  'nvkvm_dispatch.c',
+  'nvkvm_frontend.c',
+  'nvkvm_objects.c',
+  'nvkvm_mmap_host.c',
+  'nvkvm_handle.c',
+  'nvkvm_isolate.c',
+  'nvkvm_isolate_handlers.c',
+  'nvkvm_tables.c',
+  'nvkvm_present_egl.c',
+))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_LASI', if_true: files('lasi.c'))
